# Radial Color Palette Upgrade

Replace the legacy linear hue slider and fixed color presets with a professional radial color wheel for more intuitive customization.

## Proposed Changes

### [Component Name]
#### [MODIFY] [gauge_mini_settings.dart](file:///c:/projects/claude+antigravity/projects/car_dash/lib/presentation/widgets/gauge_mini_settings.dart)
- Remove `_predefinedColors` and [_presetColor](file:///c:/projects/claude+antigravity/projects/car_dash/lib/presentation/widgets/gauge_mini_settings.dart#198-215) logic.
- Remove the "HUE" slider from [_AdvancedColorPanel](file:///c:/projects/claude+antigravity/projects/car_dash/lib/presentation/widgets/gauge_mini_settings.dart#253-331).
- Implement `_HueWheelPainter` to render a conic gradient circle.
- Implement `_RadialHuePicker` widget to handle touch gestures on the wheel.
- Integrate `_RadialHuePicker` into the color configuration section.
- Maintain Glow and Opacity sliders below the radial wheel.

### [Component Name]
#### [MODIFY] [main.dart](file:///c:/projects/claude+antigravity/projects/car_dash/lib/main.dart)
- Wrap the background `Stack` in a `GestureDetector`.
- Implement tap-to-deselect logic to close settings when clicking on empty space.
- Ensure tap events on gauges still work and don't trigger background deselect.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- None (Visual UI change).

### Manual Verification
- Open gauge settings.
- Verify the 6 legacy color buttons are gone.
- Use the radial wheel to change colors.
- Verify color updates in real-time on the gauge.
- Verify glow and opacity still work correctly with the new palette.
